// The machine-readable identity of a model construct: the id it is keyed on and,
// where the two differ, the internal name it is known by.
//
// They sit at the meta level, beside the classes above, because their subjects are
// model constructs — a component type, a reference type, a field type — rather than
// the individuals a customer created. An individual carries the same two facts under
// CommonIDIRI and CommonNameIRI, which are built-in *fields*: a component really does
// have a field Ardoq calls "Ardoq OID", and advanced search filters on it. Describing
// a field type with those would have said a field type has fields, and would have left
// `?s common/id ?id` returning classes and individuals jumbled together.
//
// So the split is the level, not the meaning: MetaModelIDIRI answers "which model
// constructs are there", CommonIDIRI answers "which things are there".
const (
	MetaModelIDIRI   = MetaModelNamespace + "id"
	MetaModelNameIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "name"
)

// The legacy identifiers a concrete type carries so that Ardoq's pre-GraphLake
// code can find its way from an entity to the model and type ids it already
// holds. A component row carries `typeId` and `model`; a reference row carries
// `type` and `model`; neither is resolvable without the type row, so the type
// publishes both and one property path answers it:
//
//	?component rdf:type/aqModel:modelId         ?modelId .
//	?component rdf:type/aqModel:componentTypeId ?componentTypeId .
//
// This is a compatibility bridge. Code written against GraphLake should use the
// type IRI, which is minted from the `_id` and is unique on its own; these two are
// only meaningful as a pair, because the model-local id repeats across models.
//
// The model is not a resource. Nothing in Ardoq's model rows is worth a node here
// beyond the id, and minting one would put a class in the graph that no query asked
// for.
//
// MetaModelComponentTypeIDIRI carries `component_type.id` and
// MetaModelReferenceTypeIDIRI carries `reference_type.id` — the model-local ids,
// not the `_id`. Note that this is the opposite of what those two words mean in
// Ardoq's own schema, where a `componentTypeId` column matches `component_type._id`
// (see sourceColumnTypesByTable and the field-constraint join tables). The names
// here are the ones the consumer asked for; the `_id` is on MetaModelIDIRI.
const (
	MetaModelModelIDIRI         = MetaModelNamespace + "modelId"
	MetaModelComponentTypeIDIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "componentTypeId"
	MetaModelReferenceTypeIDIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "referenceTypeId"
)

// What a field is, beyond its identity: the value type Ardoq gives it, how it is
// formatted, where it sits in a model's field list, and which field type a model
// field is an appearance of. Advanced search reads all four.
const (
	// MetaModelFieldTypeIRI is Ardoq's own name for a field's value type — "Number",
	// "SelectMultipleList", "Url" — carried verbatim from global_field.type.
	//
	// It is published alongside the SHACL sh:datatype rather than instead of it,
	// because the two answer different questions and the datatype cannot answer this
	// one: fieldValueRange collapses Text, TextArea, List, SelectMultipleList, Email,
	// User and File all onto xsd:string. A consumer choosing an editor or a filter
	// for a field needs the distinction the range throws away.
	MetaModelFieldTypeIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "fieldType"

	// MetaModelNumberFormatOptionsIRI carries global_field.numberFormatOptions as one
	// string of JSON.
	//
	// One literal rather than a predicate per option: the option set is Ardoq's and
	// this repo does not own it, so decomposing it would invent vocabulary here and
	// silently drop whatever Ardoq adds next. The lexical form is canonicalised —
	// see canonicalJSONObject — because the snapshot path reads jsonb as Postgres
	// serialises it and the CDC path reads it as a decoded map, and two spellings of
	// the same object would churn a delete/insert on every update that did not
	// change it.
	MetaModelNumberFormatOptionsIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "numberFormatOptions"

	// MetaModelOrderIRI is a field's position in one model's field list,
	// field_id_by_model._order. Its subject is a ModelField, never a field type.
	MetaModelOrderIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "order"

	// MetaModelFieldIRI links a ModelField to the field type it is an appearance of.
	//
	// Not "fieldType", which is taken by the value type above. The two would be a
	// word apart and mean quite different things, and this one is the edge.
	MetaModelFieldIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "field"
)

// How a component type is drawn: the four style values on component_type, which
// are the defaults every component of that type inherits unless it overrides
// them. The per-component override is the CommonColorIRI group below.
//
// They are at the meta level rather than under common/ because their subject is a
// model construct, not one of the individuals common/ describes — the same split
// that puts MetaModelIDIRI on a type and CommonIDIRI on a component. A component
// type already carries rdfs:label and rdfs:comment where a component carries
// common/name and common/description, and this follows that.
//
// Keeping the two levels apart is also what makes an override recoverable. One
// shared predicate would say a component is #ff0000 and its type is #ff0000 with
// nothing to distinguish "set on this component" from "inherited", and the
// consumer this exists for needs to know which it is looking at. Resolving the
// effective value is one COALESCE over the two:
//
//	OPTIONAL { ?c aqCommon:icon ?own }
//	OPTIONAL { ?c rdf:type/aqModel:icon ?default }
//	BIND(COALESCE(?own, ?default) AS ?icon)
//
// Their subject is the concrete component type, never the name-level class: that
// class is shared by every model with a type of that name, so a colour on it
// would be multi-valued with nothing to say whose it is. Same reason
// MetaModelModelIDIRI is concrete-only.
//
// MetaModelShapeIRI is the one to read twice: "shape" here is the renderer's
// outline for a box — `item`, `bpmn-user`, `archimate-rect-interface` — and has
// nothing to do with the SHACL shapes under ShapeNamespace. The word is Ardoq's
// column name and is kept, because a built-in's local name is its source column.
const (
	MetaModelColorIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "color"
	MetaModelIconIRI  = MetaModelNamespace + "icon"
	MetaModelImageIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "image"
	MetaModelShapeIRI = MetaModelNamespace + "shape"
)

